    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Template implementation for input data to curl during a request.</para>
<para>This handler deals with the data received from the HTTP server during a request. This implementation will typically use T=std::string and just store the received data in a string. For json/XML payloads that&apos;s probably all you need. But if you receive binary data, you may want to use a container like std::vector or std::deque in stead. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
